message.content:
This is a CBP ruling about gift stickers/labels. Self-adhesive printed labels fall under 4911.10 (trade advertising material) or 4911.91 (pictures, designs) or 4821 (paper labels of all kinds, printed). Heading 4821: "Paper or paperboard labels of all kinds, whether or not printed" — 4821.10 printed; 4821.10.20 is "Pressure-sensitive labels" in older schedules, and 4821.10.40 is other. Printed gift labels with To/From would be 4821.10. Christmas items under 9505 are festive articles, but paper stickers are not typically festive articles of that heading, because they are primarily functional labels. Printed labels in 4821.10.20 would be "Pressure-sensitive"? Actually, the HTS has 4821.10.20 "Printed: Pressure-sensitive" and 4821.10.40 "Other"; the statistical suffixes are 4821.10.2010 and 4821.10.2090? Currently I believe 4821.10.20.00 is "Printed, in sheets or rolls: Pressure sensitive", with 4821.10.40.00 "Other". I'll go with 4821.10.2000.

Alternatively, CBP could have classified in 4821.10.2000 and reasoned that the labels are printed paper labels. I'll go with that.

{"hts_code": "4821.10.2000", "reason": "The printed self-adhesive paper gift labels with To/From fields are pressure-sensitive printed paper labels of heading 4821, not festive articles of heading 9505."}
